      "actor": "owner",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/repos",
      "body": "{\"name\":\"repo\",\"visibility\":\"private\"}",
      "expectedStatus": 201
    },
    {
      "actor": "owner",
      "method": "PUT",
      "path": "/repos/owner/repo/collaborators/subject",
      "body": "{\"role\":\"admin\"}",
      "expectedStatus": 201
    }
  ],
  "call": {
    "actor": "subject",
    "method": "GET",
    "path": "/repos/owner/repo",
    "body": "",
    "expectedStatus": 200
  },
  "revoke": {
    "actor": "owner",
    "method": "DELETE",
    "path": "/repos/owner/repo/collaborators/subject",
    "body": "",
    "expectedStatus": 204
  },
  "callAgain": {
    "actor": "subject",
    "method": "GET",
    "path": "/repos/owner/repo",
    "body": "",
    "expectedStatus": 404
  },
  "rationale": "With a private repo, only a role lets the subject see it. A fresh per-request evaluation means the subject's next GET after revocation has no role and gets 404. B's per-session role cache keeps the previously seen admin role, so the same GET returns 200 and the probe fails. If A's revoke did nothing, the subject would still be a collaborator and the second GET would also return 200, so the probe depends on the revoke taking effect. In base and B the DELETE route does not exist, so the revoke step hits Hono's default 404 text/plain and the probe reports n/a."
}

